   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Post-stratification weighting is often (but not always) a component of the weights accompanying survey data - see <a href=\"http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/weightingfinal.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/weightingfinal.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463111644000&amp;usg=AOvVaw01MTUeI8L5xRXr4tm03pLx\">here </a>for distinction. I&#39;m specifically thinking about simulating quantities from the model for a different distribution of covariates.<div><br></div><div>Examples:</div><div><a href=\"http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/survey_methodology.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/survey_methodology.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463111644000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hoq9h14Eb3aDNk0xoJEki\">http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/survey_methodology.pdf</a><br></div><div><a href=\"http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/Si_et_al-BA14.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/Si_et_al-BA14.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463111644000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1z7ka2et0aM1Hi0kH32Wk0\">http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/Si_et_al-BA14.pdf</a><br></div><div><a href=\"http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/KennedyGelman_manuscript.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/KennedyGelman_manuscript.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792463111644000&amp;usg=AOvVaw386u4f07OjU-heYfGGQ8KD\">http://www.stat.columbia.edu/~gelman/research/published/KennedyGelman_manuscript.pdf</a><br></div><div><a href=